# Passwordless root for exactly the two tools that need raw device access, and
# nothing else.
#
# Telegraf itself keeps running as the unprivileged `telegraf` user that the
# upstream entrypoint drops to. Only `smartctl` and `nvme` cross into root, and
# only when inputs.smartctl or inputs.smart is configured with `use_sudo = true`.
# See README.md, "Root or sudo", for why the image does not simply run Telegraf
# as root.
#
# Each tool is listed twice because sudo matches the command path *literally*,
# not after resolving symlinks: a rule naming /usr/sbin/smartctl does not
# authorize /usr/bin/smartctl even though the latter is a symlink to it. Alpine
# installs both tools under /usr/sbin, which is where inputs.smartctl looks;
# inputs.smart defaults to /usr/bin instead, and the Dockerfile adds symlinks
# there so both plugins work without being told where to look. Those symlinks
# are only reachable through sudo if the policy names them, hence four entries
# for two binaries.
#
# No argument list is pinned: these plugins call smartctl with a scan, a
# per-device query and a `--nocheck` mode whose arguments depend on plugin
# configuration, and inputs.smart additionally calls vendor-specific `nvme`
# subcommands when `enable_extensions` is on — so an argument whitelist would
# have to be re-derived on every Telegraf release. Restricting *which* binaries
# may be run is the boundary that holds; both of these read and write storage
# devices by design, so constraining their arguments would buy little even if it
# were stable.
telegraf ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/sbin/smartctl, /usr/sbin/nvme, \
                              /usr/bin/smartctl, /usr/bin/nvme

# Telegraf runs with no controlling terminal under tini, and the container has
# no resolvable hostname. Neither default applies in a container; both would
# otherwise turn every sudo call into an error.
Defaults:telegraf !requiretty
Defaults:telegraf !fqdn

# Keep the environment sudo hands the tools minimal and predictable rather than
# inheriting Telegraf's.
Defaults:telegraf secure_path="/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin"
